<title>SWITZERLAND: ACI says Jan-April 97 air cargo up 8.9 percent.</title>
<headline>ACI says Jan-April 97 air cargo up 8.9 percent.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freight and mail traffic handled by 496 airports around the world in January-April 1997, totalled 17,026,022 tonnes, up 8.9 percent on the same period the previous year, according to figures issued by Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>Cargo traffic handled by airports in ACI's six geographical regions in January-April 1997, in tonnes, with percentage change on January-April 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p>			Jan-April		  Pct Change on</p>
<p>			1997(tonnes)	     Jan-April 1996</p>
<p>Africa		   64,981		  up  1.1</p>
<p>Asia/Pacific	3,783,840		  up 13.9</p>
<p>Europe		3,419,080		  up  4.6</p>
<p>LatAm/Caribbean     387,554		  up  1.9</p>
<p>Middle East	   616,109		  up  7.6</p>
<p>N.America	   8,754,458		  up  9.1</p>
<p>    Total	  17,026,022		  up  8.9</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
</text>
